atlas creator-render

architecture creator-render-program
  canonical_name CreatorRenderProgram
  family surface
  domain Creator / Revision-scoped timeline compilation
  layer surface
  semantic_question Can a timeline become exact bounded render windows without materializing media or inferring execution authority?
  purpose Validates timeline metadata, applies revision-bound candidate edits and compiles selected frame windows with exact rational sample coordinates. A used-source projection carries only the source bases needed by the selected windows.
  maturity measured
  source_lineage Nickgonzales76017/bonfyre commit 1187f3736ebbdeba3b70edb39f04de15c752cd5c; imported files and exact upstream digests retained in packs/no-simulation/creator-upstream-20261013/sources.json
  source_path Aurekai/src/creator-render-program.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/src/creator-native-pcm.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/src/creator-cli.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/bin/akai.mjs
  internal_calculus an immutable prepared clip index selects window overlaps; BigInt frame-to-sample arithmetic rounds each rational boundary once
  invariant timeline edits name the exact previous digest and return an uncommitted candidate; compile and PCM-plan commands read bounded metadata only and never read source PCM or execute a renderer
  invariant PCM lowering requires exact declared source digests and absolute paths but marks those claims unverified until an execution owner checks bytes
  witness Aurekai/tests/creator-render-program.test.mjs exercises exact cuts, revision checks, source projection and prepared-index behavior across synthetic 10k-clip and 6000-source fixtures
  witness Aurekai/tests/creator-native-pcm.test.mjs checks candidate lowering and exact native arithmetic under explicit synthetic test execution
  witness Aurekai/tests/creator-cli.test.mjs verifies reachable repository CLI commands, immutable input, stale edit refusal, missing media allowed for planning and refusal of oversized or nonregular metadata
  forbidden_inference a valid scope digest or candidate argv -> authenticated authority, media rights, source-byte verification or a completed render
  known_gap the global akai executable points to a separate checkout; these commands are wired into this repository's CLI only. No interactive editor or media decoder is supplied by this compiler

architecture cmd-creator-mix
  canonical_name BonfyreCreatorMix
  family command
  domain Creator / Native offline audio
  layer command
  semantic_question Can an explicitly invoked native operation mix a bounded audio window with exact ordered float32 arithmetic and sparse silent output?
  purpose Mixes up to 64 interleaved f32le stems in 1024-frame blocks, scheduling active stems by ordered start/end events. Sparse silence is opt-in and retains byte-equivalent logical output.
  maturity measured
  command BonfyreCreatorMix
  source_lineage native mixer and allocation-free kernel imported unchanged from Nickgonzales76017/bonfyre commit 1187f3736ebbdeba3b70edb39f04de15c752cd5c
  source_path Aurekai/native/creator/mix.c
  source_path Aurekai/native/creator/mix_kernel.c
  source_path Aurekai/native/creator/mix_kernel.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/Makefile
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tools/demo.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tools/demo.html
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tests/browser.mjs
  internal_calculus time events maintain a 64-bit active set, iterated in original stem order; consecutive source blocks reuse their stream position; unoccupied output blocks may become sparse file holes
  invariant the local build disables fast-math and floating-point contraction to preserve ordered float32 accumulation and nonfinite refusal
  invariant output is published without overwriting an existing path; receipts describe materialized_unverified output and never infer execution authority
  witness Aurekai/tests/creator-native-mix.test.mjs checks exact samples, short and nonfinite input refusal, offset boundaries, 64-stem event scheduling, sparse parity and sequential seek elision
  witness packs/no-simulation/creator-upstream-20261013/demo/verification.json verifies every output float32 sample against an independent reference, source digests before and after rendering and byte-identical dense/sparse output for a six-second stereo fixture
  witness cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tests/browser.mjs verifies actual WAV decode and playback, no script exceptions and desktop/phone layouts for the retained synthetic preview
  forbidden_inference a materialized mix or a source size check -> verified source digest, rights, authorization, a live audio engine or a finished DAW
  known_gap raw PCM input only, with no codec decoding, source-digest enforcement, effects, recording or real-time playback in this executable; the same kernel has a separately verified browser WASM adapter

interaction creator-plan-lowers-native-pcm
  source creator-render-program
  destination cmd-creator-mix
  relation exact_window_to_unexecuted_native_candidate
  preserves timeline and scope digests, selected window body key, stem order, integer sample coordinates and explicit source binding claims
  drops unrelated source bases and automatic execution
  forbidden_inference successful lowering -> permission to invoke the renderer or verification of the bound files
  invalidates_on timeline, scope, source bindings, frame clock or native PCM contract changing
  witness Aurekai/tests/creator-native-pcm.test.mjs
  binding Aurekai/src/creator-native-pcm.mjs


architecture creator-browser-mix
  canonical_name CreatorBrowserMix
  family surface
  domain Creator / Browser offline audio
  layer surface
  semantic_question Can the unchanged native audio kernel render bounded browser blocks with byte-exact native parity?
  purpose Runs the shared C kernel as a pinned WASM artifact behind a browser-safe block adapter. A local synthetic sample exposes gain controls and Web Audio playback.
  maturity measured
  source_path Aurekai/src/creator-wasm.mjs
  source_path Aurekai/native/creator/mix_kernel.wasm
  source_path Aurekai/native/creator/wasm.lock.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tools/wasm.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tools/wasm-demo.html
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tools/wasm-demo.mjs
  internal_calculus two bounded scratch buffers above the exported heap base preserve ordered float32 multiply/add; no fast-math or contraction; at most 1024 frames, eight channels and 64 stems per call
  invariant artifact and source digests are verified without a runtime compiler; Zig 0.13.0 reproduces the reviewed artifact byte for byte
  invariant WASM has no host imports and fixed 128 KiB linear memory; returned Float32Array blocks and caller-owned media require additional JavaScript memory
  witness Aurekai/tests/creator-wasm.test.mjs verifies native byte parity across one, two and eight channels with 64 overlapping stems, bounds refusal, nonfinite and overflow refusal, recovery, independent outputs and impossible memory growth
  witness cmd/BonfyreCreatorMix/tests/wasm-browser.mjs checks all 576000 output values against native bytes in Chrome, gain mute/reset, playback and stop, no script exceptions and desktop/phone layouts
  witness packs/no-simulation/creator-wasm-20261013/browser-verification.json retains actual browser evidence for the six-second synthetic fixture
  forbidden_inference byte parity or a short offline render -> real-time audio guarantees, media rights, verified source identity, AudioWorklet integration or public deployment
  known_gap caller owns loading and scheduling; source PCM and full output are resident in the sample; no worker, effects, recording or streaming decoder

interaction creator-native-kernel-to-browser
  source cmd-creator-mix
  destination creator-browser-mix
  relation shared_c_kernel_compiled_to_wasm
  preserves ordered float32 arithmetic, interleaved channel layout, bounded block coordinates and nonfinite output refusal
  drops native filesystem IO, event scheduling, source cursors, sparse output and native materialization receipts
  forbidden_inference shared kernel -> equivalent filesystem semantics, execution authority or complete native renderer behavior
  invalidates_on C kernel, compiler flags, artifact digest or adapter ABI changing
  witness Aurekai/tests/creator-wasm.test.mjs
  binding Aurekai/src/creator-wasm.mjs


architecture service-creator-audio
  canonical_name ServiceSiteCreatorAudio
  family surface
  domain Creator / Public sample workspace
  layer surface
  semantic_question Can a visitor import or select recordings, edit their timeline, retain the source session and export a mix through the existing native kernel?
  purpose Packages a verified synthetic sample and runs imported WAV clips through the same native kernel in a module worker. Separate source, timeline and export views retain original recordings, edits and source identities in the existing browser store.
  maturity measured
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/creator.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-material.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-sample.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-worker.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-import.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-import-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-import-view.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-timeline.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator-timeline-model.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/vendor/wavesurfer-8.0.2/provenance.tsv
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/creator-timeline.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/creator-timeline-browser.mjs
  invariant arrangement gestures and source waveform regions project into the existing integer-frame clip contract; only the native WASM renderer produces mixed audio, and persisted sessions retain the existing expected-revision record
  invariant WaveSurfer 8.0.2 and Regions are self-hosted with their BSD-3-Clause license inside the content-addressed audio package; they receive validated source peaks without audio uploads or a second playback engine
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/audio/local-arrangement/verification.json records pointer and keyboard arrangement edits, waveform region trim, undo and redo, synchronized zoom and scroll, cursor playback, reload, mobile fit and independently calculated exported PCM
  forbidden_inference waveform editing and a populated arrangement -> account synchronization, collaborative editing, long-form production audio or completion of the other demo programs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/creator-import.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/creator-import-browser.mjs
  invariant imported WAV input is bounded to eight tracks and 24 MB encoded, with at most 32 MB decoded PCM; only PCM16 or float32 mono/stereo with one sample rate and clips within a 30-second timeline are admitted
  invariant browser session saves retain source bytes and fingerprints through the existing expected-revision store; restores verify each source before rendering, and a replacement recording set does not inherit the prior permission statement
  invariant imported render requests name their worker session; late replacement cannot silently render an earlier editor's clips against another recording set
  witness 2026-10-15 creator-import.test.mjs independently checks every rendered sample for trim, placement, gain and mute; it also verifies WAV bounds, source fingerprints, same-rate admission, nonfinite rejection and clipping reports
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/creator.css
  source_path packs/aurekai-work-samples/audio/sample.json
  source_path packs/aurekai-work-samples/site/material.mjs
  internal_calculus ordered native-kernel blocks render in a module worker; the client coalesces newer gain requests, transfers completed output and caches the waveform between playback frames
  invariant packaged sample initialization verifies source hashes and the initial native reference before enabling playback; imports retain separately hashed source WAVs and do not borrow that synthetic native-reference claim
  invariant saved levels use the existing browser workbench store with expected revisions and the sample ID plus native output digest; stale tabs cannot overwrite newer levels
  invariant audio modules and source files share a content-addressed asset directory so a new deployment cannot reuse stale module URLs
  invariant WAV export is signed 16-bit PCM with explicit clipping; parity with native float32 applies before that export conversion
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/creator.test.mjs checks exact native output, every WAV sample, source-drift refusal and package bounds
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/creator-browser.mjs checks initial native parity, edits, reload, stale-tab refusal, playback, stop, a decoded and physically downloaded WAV, invalid worker input, missing and corrupted assets and responsive layouts
  witness packs/no-simulation/creator-site-20261013/local/verification.json retains eighteen browser checks with no server writes or script exceptions
  witness packs/no-simulation/creator-site-20261013/live/verification.json retains sixteen successful checks on the published audio route, including browser Back, saved levels, stale-tab refusal and actual WAV download
  witness packs/no-simulation/creator-site-20261013/public-readback.json independently matches all thirteen published HTML, CSS and versioned audio-package files to the reviewed build
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/audio/local-desk/verification.json retains 28 successful imported-session browser checks, including independent downloaded PCM values, two sample rates, source tampering, invalid import recovery, stale tabs and 320 to 1440 pixel layouts; the original sample passes all eighteen browser checks in packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/audio/regression/verification.json
  forbidden_inference generated-tone parity or browser-local saves -> rights over third-party media, live collaborative editing, real-time audio guarantees or a complete DAW
  known_gap decoded PCM and mixed output remain resident in bounded memory; longer recordings, other codecs, effects, live recording, multiple imported-session libraries, account sync and an AudioWorklet engine remain unimplemented

